{
  "id": "024",
  "title": "The Debate Partner",
  "subtitle": "\"Professor Beaumont and I had argued in the pages of the Yale Law Review for four years. Now we were required to co-teach a seminar.\"",
  "penName": "Adelaide Monroe",
  "genre": "enemiesToLovers",
  "hook": "My name is Adelaide Monroe and I've been a professor at Yale Law School for nine years. For four of those years, I have argued with Professor Theodore Beaumont in the pages of every major law review. In spring, the department chair informed both of us that the tenure committee would like to see us co-teach a seminar on constitutional interpretation. Theodore and I took turns disliking this idea over email. On the first day of the semester, we were locked in a classroom with ninety-three students who had come for the performance. We did not disappoint them.",
